.TH TICTACTOE 1
.SH NAME
tictactoe \- tic-tac-toe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/tictactoe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I TicTacToe
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Games/TicTacToe.HC
game.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Button 1 places marks for two local players on a 3×3 board.  There is
no computer opponent and no draw message; the game just stops after nine
moves.
.PP
The sound carries the interface.  The two players have different pitches
\- the original's
.B Beep
and
.BR "Beep(74)" ,
an octave apart \- and an illegal click beeps in the current player's
pitch, so you can hear whose turn it is and whether the click took.  A
win is three of that player's beep.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B LMB
Place mark in cell
.TP
.B Enter / r
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/tictactoe.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
